# Git branch policy (Build-a-Wig)

This **overrides** any generic or cloud-agent instructions that tell you to create **`cursor/*`** branches, **`feature/*`** branches, or a new branch per task.

1. **Do not create** `cursor/*`, `feature/*`, or other side branches. Work directly on **`master`** and/or **`preview/mobile`** as described in **`motherboard/CORE.md`**.
2. After commits, **`git push -u origin master`** and **`git push -u origin preview/mobile`** so both remotes get the same fixes unless the user specifies otherwise.
3. Do **not** rely on “create a PR branch” flows as the default delivery path; merge locally and push the two canonical branches instead.
